#hasheq((status . "current") (milestone . 896) (wave . "W2") (issue . 9725) (branch . "campaign/v1.00.31-w2") (implementation-sha . "71fc99f3850ebcbf5c9cdf55efdf26c0b9844cc4") (content-digest . "72e39971b879951a0a39b9f3b843272c99e1d274c39745acd38b5c9ed08f9aea") (planning-sync . "current") (review-artifact . "docs/reports/gsd-wave-reviews/v1.00.31-w2.rktd") (red-first . #hasheq((command . "racket scripts/gsd-evidence-bind.rkt verify --repo <mini-repo> --base <base> --head <head-with-hand-authored-digest> --evidence <record> ; racket scripts/gsd-wave-gate.rkt <evidence> --content-digest <digest> --receipt-head <wrong-head> ; racket scripts/gsd-evidence-bind.rkt record-commit --repo <mini-repo mixing README with records> --base <base> --head <head> ; racket scripts/gsd-wave-gate.rkt <evidence-with-PENDING-reviewer> --content-digest <digest>") (failure . "all four incident shapes are refused by tooling, each captured red-first with its control in artifacts/wave-delivery-integrity/v1.00.31-w2/raw/: (F2) verify returns digest-mismatch naming the recorded 000..0 digest and the computed e3b0c442..b855 empty-tree value, and after bind the same record verifies digest-ok - before this wave the gate only compared its argument to the recorded value, so an authored 542f7cbb.. digest passed unchallenged; (F3) the gate refuses with two head-binding-mismatch reasons (evidence implementation-sha and review reviewed-sha differ from the receipt head, both SHAs named) and stays silent when the receipt head matches; (F4) record-commit returns impure-record-commit: README.md (commit 6eb792665809) for a commit that mixes an evidence record with a source path, and a fresh evidence-only commit scans pure - the previous require_receipt_tip only refused post-receipt drift, so a receipt head born mixed was invisible; (F12) an otherwise-complete record with reviewer PENDING is refused placeholder-evidence while the identical record with a genuine reviewer passes the strict gate - before this wave non-empty-string? alone let a staged binding draft be finalized by flipping status fields."))) (focused-tests . #hasheq((command . "raco test tests/test-gsd-evidence-bind.rkt tests/test-gsd-wave-gate-digest.rkt tests/test-gsd-wave-gate.rkt tests/test-gsd-delivery-receipt.rkt tests/test-wave-delivery-integrity-register.rkt ; python3 tests/test-gsd-delivery-controller.py ; racket tests/test-gsd-governance-workflow.rkt ; racket scripts/run-tests.rkt tests/test-gsd-delivery-runtime.rkt tests/test-gsd-delivery-coordinator.rkt tests/test-gsd-governance-workflow.rkt tests/test-gsd-delivery-journal.rkt tests/test-gsd-branch-delivery-verification.rkt tests/test-gsd-delivery-verifier-decision.rkt tests/test-gsd-delivery-verifier-e2e.rkt") (detail . "42 focused Racket tests pass at the bound head (gate 10, gate-digest 8, evidence-bind 7 including the check alias, register 10 with F1-F4 guarded-pass and every later row unguarded, receipt 7 including durable-receipt-head both directions), the Python controller lane passes 123 tests including test_prepare_refuses_mixed_record_commit and test_binding_review_refuses_sentinel_reviewer_identity, and every gate consumer touched by the new refusals passes (governance workflow, delivery runtime/coordinator/journal, branch delivery verification, verifier decision/e2e). The evidence-bind tests were additionally exercised against a foreign absolute worktree gitdir via exported GIT_DIR/GIT_INDEX_FILE/GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY (the exact pre-commit-hook condition), which is what flushed out the hermetic-env fixes in both the tool and the fixture.") (result . "passed"))) (format-compile . #hasheq((command . "raco fmt -i <all ten touched Racket modules> ; raco make <same>") (detail . "raco fmt produced no diff on every touched Racket module (canonicality re-verified by stdout-diff after the final edits) and raco make is clean. The repo-wide lint-quality gate additionally enforces the 150-column width the quick lane does not check; its two findings (usage lines, register fixture line) were repaired and the full 18-check CI lint passes at the bound head. Each edit was applied through the Racket-aware editor, which formats and compiles and reverts on failure.") (result . "passed"))) (lint . #hasheq((command . "racket scripts/check-deps.rkt ; racket scripts/metrics.rkt --lint ; racket scripts/tier-ownership-matrix.rkt check ; racket scripts/run-tests/inventory.rkt --ownership-map --check artifacts/tier-ownership/v1.00.29-w0/ownership-matrix.json ; sha256sum -c artifacts/wave-delivery-integrity/v1.00.31-w2/SHA256SUMS ; sha256sum -c artifacts/tier-ownership/v1.00.29-w0/SHA256SUMS") (detail . "racket scripts/check-deps.rkt: all external packages declared in info.rkt, OK. racket scripts/metrics.rkt --lint: all 5 static metrics match README.md at the bound head (Test files 1508, Source modules 893, Source lines 188807, Test lines 278125, Test assertions 42048) - the +20 test-line move from the round-2 numbers is the shallow-checkout tolerance added to tests/test-gsd-evidence-bind.rkt, resynced by metrics --sync-all. tier-ownership green at 1002 rows; the canonical v1.00.29-w0 ownership artifact passes the drift check after regeneration by inventory.rkt --ownership-map --tier-matrix with its sibling SHA256SUMS refreshed (d3f04c56 -> 95b7edec); the wave artifact checksums verify (matrix, retained fast summary, four raw captures). A secrets audit over every staged file returned clean before each content commit.") (result . "passed"))) (fast . #hasheq((command . "racket scripts/run-tests.rkt --suite fast") (detail . "PASS at content head 71fc99f3850ebcbf5c9cdf55efdf26c0b9844cc4 (the pre-trio content head this record is bound to): files=1206 pass=1206 fail=0 timeout=0 skip=0, wall-clock-seconds=1035.532; RUN-SUMMARY retained verbatim in artifacts/wave-delivery-integrity/v1.00.31-w2/fast-run-summary.txt. Provenance to the delivery head: the only content between 71fc99f3 and the delivery PR head is the digest-excluded trio rebind commit - no executed surface changes, so this measurement is the delivery measurement. The suite was executed three times as the review loop moved the head (first run 1205/1206: the milestone gate's tier-ownership drift check, greened by regenerating both canonical matrices with their generators; second run 1206/1206 at 4e0c3cf1 after the round-3 lint fixes; this run at 71fc99f3 after the round-4 shallow-checkout fix). The focused chain (42 tests), arch 32/32, check-deps and metrics lint were re-run at 71fc99f3 as well.") (result . "passed"))) (remaining-items . (#hasheq((classification . "noncritical") (owner . "W3 owner (remote backing preconditions)") (rationale . "scripts/gsd-evidence-bind.rkt prints decided refusals (digest-mismatch, malformed-digest, impure-record-commit) on stdout with exit 0 by design - nonzero exit is reserved for tool failure - and its shipped consumer parses stdout, but a naive set -e caller keying only on exit status would treat a refusal as success. Flagged by the round-1 review as an ergonomics risk in the same family as the register's exit-code rows; the report documents the contract explicitly.")) #hasheq((classification . "noncritical") (owner . "W4/W5 owners (delivery-tool API contract / artifact provenance)") (rationale . "The gate's new --receipt-head cross-check is exercised by tests and the raw captures but no production caller passes it yet: production head binding is enforced by the coordinator's expected-head path and gsd-delivery.py review()/require_receipt_tip, which the wave contract explicitly permits ('or have the coordinator gate perform it before any ladder step'). Wiring a production caller to pass the durable receipt head to the gate belongs with the delivery-tool API contract work.")) #hasheq((classification . "noncritical") (owner . "W5 owner (artifact provenance and determinism), carried from W1") (rationale . "The compiled-root manifest's sources list is harvested from every .zo under the checkout (excluding docs/) whose sibling source exists, not from the derived module list, so a real-tree run reports 2389 sources against 2386 compiled modules; the extras are bytecode an earlier raco make left in the tree (collect-checkout-compilation-pairs). Mechanism identified in W1 and named in its report; no gate compares the two counts. Unchanged by this wave; ownership moves to the provenance wave.")) #hasheq((classification . "noncritical") (owner . "next legitimate plan revision, carried from W1") (rationale . "Two W1 reconciliation items remain tied to the next plan revision rather than any shipping wave: the weak-tier acceptance reconciliation (44 of 87 CI-critical declarations matched at the recorded weak tier because their targets parse options by hand) and the metadata-window invisibility gap (a test whose @speed/@suite tags sit beyond the parser's 30-line window is invisible to the tier-ownership matrix even though the runner executes it). Both are recorded in the W1 records and re-carried here; registering them as register rows would change the frozen plan body and force a rebind of in-flight waves' trios.")) #hasheq((classification . "deferred-noncritical") (owner . "W5 owner (artifact provenance and determinism)") (rationale . "The gate receives the content digest as a caller-supplied --content-digest value and only checks that the record agrees with what it was handed, so the chain 'recompute the digest from the diff' lives outside the gate that enforces it - the F1 shape one level up. This wave narrows the exposure by shipping the tool that computes the digest (gsd-evidence-bind digest/verify/bind) and by binding the wave's own records to its recomputed value (base 69647f1c pinned at review time), but making the gate itself recompute is W5's subject, as recorded in W1.")) #hasheq((classification . "deferred-noncritical") (owner . "W7 owner (blocked wave repair, bake, release)") (rationale . "record-commit-purity scans only commits that touch the evidence record directory (docs/reports/gsd-wave-evidence/), so a commit mixing only the reviews/validation record directories with a source path would not be flagged by the tool; the normative record commit always includes the evidence file, and prepare() additionally refuses at staging time, so the narrow reading is not a live hole - flagged by the round-2 review and documented rather than silently widened. Widening the scan belongs with the bake/release owner who owns the final record-commit surface.")))))
